            "source": "Hacker News",
            "category": "technology",
            "title": "Show HN: macOS data protection keychain for Electron apps",
            "description": "<p>Hey HN,<p>I've been working on Hansel [1] (an encrypted personal data store you can query with agents), and there wasn't a good way to use the modern macOS Data Protection Keychain.<p>Electron's safeStorage [2] uses the legacy file-based keychain, which allows other apps/agents to query it with the `security` CLI. Not great when you have a dozen agents running in the background! The Data Protection Keychain is nice because it limits access via code-signing access groups and lets you set access rules like Touch ID and/or password.<p>1: <a href=\"https://hansel.so/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://hansel.so/</a><p>2. <a href=\"https://www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/api/safe-storage\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/api/safe-storage</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49349159\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49349159</a></p>\n<p>Points: 3</p>\n<p># Comments: 0</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/biw/keychain-store",
            "published": "Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:25:19 +0000",
            "fetched": "2026-08-18T21:51:43+03:30"
        },
